# Black Bean Burger

Based on [https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/…](https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/black-bean-burgers/15322) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20211023023225/https://www.washingtonpost.com/recipes/black-bean-burgers/15322))

{ rating="5" image="black_bean_burger.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2x 15-oz cans of [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, drained and rinsed
- [ ] Generous 1 cup [chickpea flour]{ ing="chickpea-flour" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [plain]{ ing="plain" }, unsweetened applesauce
- [ ] 1 tsp [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [tamari]{ ing="tamari" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [apple cider vinegar]{ ing="apple-cider-vinegar" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp fresh [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] [Vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" }, for shallow frying
- [ ] 8 [whole wheat buns]{ ing="whole-wheat-buns" }
- [ ] [Toppings such as cheese]{ ing="toppings-such-as-cheese" }, slices of tomato or onion, pickles, mustard and/or ketchup

## Recipe

1. Use a fork to mash the [beans]{ ing="black-beans" } in a large mixing bowl so they’re mushy but not totally smooth. There should still be some whole beans in the mixture
1. Add the [chickpea flour]{ ing="chickpea-flour" }, [tomato paste]{ ing="tomato-paste" }, applesauce, [chili powder]{ ing="chili-powder" }, [tamari]{ ing="tamari" }, [vinegar]{ ing="apple-cider-vinegar" }, [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, stirring to incorporate
1. In a skillet, pour a thin layer of [oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" } and heat on medium heat
1. Place a generous 1/3 cup of the mixture in the center of the pan. Carefully press it into a round, pressing until the patty is about 3/4 inch thick. Repeat to form 2-4 burgers
1. Cook until browned and crisp on both sides (1-2 min per side). Flip as needed so that they cook evenly
1. Serve on [buns]{ ing="whole-wheat-buns" }, with [cheese]{ ing="toppings-such-as-cheese" }, slices of tomato and onion, pickles, mustard, and/or ketchup
